{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "ArcCivs internal resources and external economy assessment (static source model)",
  "assumptions": [
    "This is a source-derived before/after model, not a live-server observation. Before means no ArcCivs flows; after means the source-defined rules, not proof of a deployed plugin.",
    "participants [1, 10, 16] mean active settlement owners with a nearby viewer during the assumed work window, not registered accounts or measured concurrent users.",
    "Per active owner-day ceilings: low = one L1 producer for one hour (60 trips); base = one L2 producer for two hours (120 trips); high = three L3 producer workers for four hours (720 trips). These are theoretical trip bounds before route time and storage-full pauses, not measured throughput.",
    "Wood, stone and food each use a separate, non-tradeable internal stock-unit namespace. Their item-kind calculator rows describe gross stock production and must not be read as Vault, token, XP or physical inventory-item emission.",
    "Each resource's low/base/high production row is an independent ceiling. The high rows reuse the same 48 active NPCs and cannot be summed as simultaneous output for all three resources.",
    "Ordinary production consumes no food. Construction and recruitment costs are shown as exact one-time internal resource costs below; no unsupported daily spending frequency is assumed.",
    "The plugin has no source-defined Vault/token payout or redemption path. Existing EconomyShopGUI SELL and AutoSellChests flows remain outside this model and are not assumed to be removed or replaced."
  ],
